  "subtitle": "Updated: Feb 17 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Acetabular Screw Placement and Safe Zones",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Draw quadrants",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/5029/images/safe%20zones%203.jpg",
              "caption": "Safe Zones 3"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "first line drawn from ASIS to center of acetabulum",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "second line drawn perpendicular to first line",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Quadrant",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**posterior-superior quadrant**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "\"target zone\"",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "is the ideal place for supplemental component screws.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "elevating the hip center in revisions can place sciatic nerve at risk in this quadrant",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**posterior-inferior quadrant**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "\"caution zone\"",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if screw exceeds 20mm the following structures are at risk",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "sciatic nerve",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "inferior gluteal nerve and vessels",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "internal pudendal nerve and vessels",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**anterior-inferior quadrant**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "\"danger zone\"",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "obturator nerve, artery, and vein at risk",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**anterior-superior quadrant**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "\"death zone\"",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "external iliac vessels at risk",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Exceptions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "in the \"high hip\" the structures in the anterosuperior and anteroinferior quadrants are often found in the posterosuperior quadrant",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Avoiding Prosthesis Impingement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Leaving the anterior rim of the acetabular component proud above the native acetabulum may result in anterior iliopsoas tendon impingement",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "evaluate with cross-table lateral radiograph and anesthetic injection of the iliopsoas tendon sheath",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Causes of impingement",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "medializing and raising acetabulum cup center of rotation will increase risk of bone-on-bone impingement by decreasing femoral offset",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "lateralizing cup will increase risk of metal femoral neck-on-metal acetabulum impingement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "femoral head-to-neck ratio (<2:1) will increase risk of impingement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "femoral head skirts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "small femoral head",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
